# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 1: mare), edited.

~ start
Narrator: A broken halter dangles from the post, and the damp straw of the third stall is still warm.
marianna_grey [afraid]: The clocktower tolled and my grey mare Clover bolted up the northern moor road. Find her before the wolves do for my goodwill and three days free horse hire.
* We will find her -> accept
* Ask what Clover is like -> about
* Not now -> END

~ about
marianna_grey [neutral]: She is gentle, just skittish around flapping cloaks. Offer a handful of dry oats and she will come to your palm.
-> start

~ accept
marianna_grey [weary]: Mind the ditches. Fog hides the ruts, and she has only one good front shoe.
quest the_grey_mare asked
set mare_asked
-> END

~ progress
marianna_grey [weary]: Empty halter in hand and wind rising. Seen hide or hair of her yet?
* Any advice? -> advice
* [ends:the_grey_mare] We could not find her -> give_up
* Leave -> END

~ advice
marianna_grey [neutral]: Tuck in your cloaks and shake a pouch of oats when close. If mud hides her prints, fetch Hilda Brom.
-> progress

~ give_up
marianna_grey [sad]: I see. Best I latch the third stall shut and save the straw for the horses left.
quest the_grey_mare lost
set mare_lost
standing patient_lady -1
-> END

~ tracks
Narrator: Crescent hoofprints score the wet peat along the northern verge, filling with black moor water.
* [Survival DC 12] Follow them -> tracks_ok | tracks_fail
* Ask Hilda Brom to track her instead -> tracks_hilda
* Leave -> END

~ tracks_ok
Narrator: Scuffed moss and snapped gorse mark a stumbling path toward a bramble thicket by the north wall.
set mare_found
quest the_grey_mare found
-> END

~ tracks_fail
Narrator: The hoofprints vanish into boggy cart ruts and sheep droppings. Hilda Brom could read this mire better.
-> END

~ tracks_hilda
hilda_brom [neutral]: Thrown left shoe, panicked stride, dragging her halter through the gorse. Check the thicket by the north wall.
set mare_found
quest the_grey_mare found
-> END

~ mare_there
Narrator: The dapple-grey mare stands tangled in wet briars by the stones, flanks heaving and ears pinned at your shadow.
* [Animal Handling DC 12] Talk her down -> catch_ok | catch_fail
* Offer oats from the pack -> catch_oats
* [Athletics DC 14] Rope her -> catch_ok | catch_fail
* Leave her -> END

~ catch_ok
Narrator: Her trembling eases at your touch, and she lowers her nose for {name} to take the frayed rope.
set mare_caught
quest the_grey_mare caught
-> END

~ catch_fail
Narrator: She snorts in terror, wrenching free to bolt down the wall. A handful of oats might steady her where quick hands failed.
-> END

~ catch_oats
Narrator: Dry grain rustles in your palm, and the mare steps from the thorns to lip oats from {name}'s fingers.
set mare_caught
quest the_grey_mare caught
-> END

~ return
Narrator: Clover presses her damp forehead to the stablemistress's shoulder, blowing a warm breath into her apron.
marianna_grey [smile]: Plastered in peat and burs, you foolish old girl. Take this coin, friends, and any horse in my yard is yours free for three days.
set mare_returned
quest the_grey_mare done
gold +25
standing patient_lady +1
-> END
